# Phase 1 RLS policy performance evidence (review HIGH 8 / MEDIUM 12)

Environment: local docker stack (postgis/postgis:16-3.5), tenant `acme`
(10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001), actor acme tenant_admin
(10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011), 100k extra sites, 100k extra users
and 100k extra memberships in that tenant.

Reproduce:
  INSERT INTO app.sites (tenant_id, name)
    SELECT '10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Perf Site ' || g
    FROM generate_series(1, 100000) g;
  INSERT INTO app.users (id, email, email_verified, display_name)
    SELECT ('20000000-0000-4000-8000-' || lpad(g::text, 12, '0'))::uuid,
           'perf-' || g || '@example.com', true, 'Perf ' || g
    FROM generate_series(1, 100000) g;
  INSERT INTO app.memberships (tenant_id, user_id, role)
    SELECT '10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
           ('20000000-0000-4000-8000-' || lpad(g::text, 12, '0'))::uuid, 'viewer'
    FROM generate_series(1, 100000) g;
  node packages/db/scripts/explain-policies.mjs plan sites
  node packages/db/scripts/explain-policies.mjs time sites 1000
  node packages/db/scripts/explain-policies.mjs full sites

## Before (0013): bare helper calls, evaluated per row

EXPLAIN (VERBOSE, COSTS OFF) SELECT count(*) FROM app.sites;

Aggregate
  Output: count(*)
  ->  Index Scan using sites_tenant_idx on app.sites
        Output: id, tenant_id, name, address, status, created_at, updated_at
        Index Cond: (sites.tenant_id = app.tenant_id())
        Filter: (app.can_manage_tenant() OR (app.actor_role() = 'viewer'::text) OR app.has_site(sites.id))

The 100k count did not finish in five minutes and the backend was terminated.
A 1,000-row subset (LIMIT 1000) still took ~2.9s because every candidate row
re-entered the helper functions:

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
SELECT count(*) FROM (SELECT 1 FROM app.sites LIMIT 1000) s;

Aggregate  (actual time=2937.379..2937.381 rows=1 loops=1)
  Buffers: shared hit=19037
  ->  Limit  (actual time=4.037..2935.930 rows=1000 loops=1)
        ->  Index Scan using sites_tenant_idx on sites
              (actual time=4.035..2934.882 rows=1000 loops=1)
              Index Cond: (tenant_id = app.tenant_id())
              Filter: (app.can_manage_tenant() OR (app.actor_role() = 'viewer'::text) OR app.has_site(id))
Execution Time: 2937.440 ms

## After (0014): helpers hoisted to InitPlans

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT count(*) FROM app.sites;  -- 100k rows

Aggregate  (cost=2475.95..2475.96 rows=1 width=8)
           (actual time=84.858..84.861 rows=1 loops=1)
  Buffers: shared hit=1652 dirtied=4
  InitPlan 1 (returns $0)
    ->  Result  (actual time=5.756..5.757 rows=1 loops=1)
  InitPlan 2 (returns $1)
    ->  Result  (actual time=4.218..4.218 rows=1 loops=1)
  InitPlan 3 (returns $2)
    ->  Result  (never executed)
  InitPlan 4 (returns $3)
    ->  Result  (never executed)
  ->  Index Scan using sites_tenant_idx on sites
        (actual time=10.025..69.220 rows=100002 loops=1)
        Index Cond: (tenant_id = $0)
        Filter: ($1 OR ($2 = 'viewer'::text) OR (id = ANY ($3)))
Execution Time: 85.069 ms

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT count(*) FROM app.memberships;  -- 100k rows

Aggregate  (actual time=53.079..53.082 rows=1 loops=1)
  InitPlan 1..3 (actor_id, tenant_id, can_manage_tenant)
  ->  Seq Scan on memberships (actual time=4.933..41.396 rows=100003 loops=1)
        Filter: ((user_id = $0) OR ((tenant_id = $1) AND $2))
Execution Time: 53.347 ms

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS) SELECT count(*) FROM app.users;  -- 100k rows

Aggregate  (actual time=741.265..741.272 rows=1 loops=1)
  InitPlan 1..2 (actor_id, can_manage_tenant)
  ->  Seq Scan on users (actual time=648.453..725.902 rows=100003 loops=1)
        Filter: ((id = $0) OR ($1 AND (hashed SubPlan 12)))
        SubPlan 12
          ->  Seq Scan on memberships m (actual time=40.574..87.187 rows=100003 loops=1)
                Filter: ((tenant_id = $8) AND ((user_id = $9) OR ((tenant_id = $10) AND $11)))
Execution Time: 1254.017 ms

The users policy is intentionally still an inline per-row membership
existence check (review MEDIUM 12): it now uses the membership expression
instead of calling app.is_user_in_tenant() per row, and all stable context
lookups are InitPlans. Total suite after 0014: 39/39.


## Round-2 follow-up: paginated list plans and write timings

Machine: Intel Core i3-4005U @ 1.70GHz (2C/4T), 7.7GiB RAM,
Linux x86_64 container host; PostgreSQL 16.9 (postgis/postgis:16-3.5);
Docker server 29.1.3; Node v24.22.2. Same 100k-row `acme` tenant as above.

Commands (page mode orders by the UI's display key and limits to 50;
`EXPLAIN_ACTOR` selects the seeded actor):

```shell
for actor in tenant_admin site_manager viewer; do
  for table in sites memberships users; do
    EXPLAIN_ACTOR=$actor node packages/db/scripts/explain-policies.mjs page $table 50
  done
done
```

Write paths (all inside one transaction, rolled back):

```sql
EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
INSERT INTO app.sites (tenant_id, name)
VALUES ('10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001', 'Perf Probe') RETURNING id;

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
UPDATE app.sites SET name = 'Perf Probe Updated'
WHERE id = '20000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001' RETURNING id;

EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
UPDATE app.memberships SET role = 'viewer'
WHERE user_id = '00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005'
  AND tenant_id = '10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001' RETURNING id;
```

